<h2>Mobile Speed Impact: Where Most Contractors Lose the Most Leads</h2>

<p>Mobile performance was the most significant differentiator in our entire study. While desktop performance still matters, the gap between mobile and desktop speed on contractor websites is where the majority of lead loss occurs. This section examines why mobile is so critical and what the data reveals about mobile-specific performance issues.</p>

<h3>The Mobile-Desktop Performance Gap</h3>

<p>Across our 100 websites, the average desktop Lighthouse Performance score was 72. The average mobile score was 54. This 18-point gap represents a massive difference in user experience. A site that feels acceptable on a fast desktop computer with a broadband connection feels sluggish and frustrating on a mobile device with variable connectivity.</p>

<p>The gap exists for several technical reasons. Mobile devices have less processing power than desktops. Mobile networks, even 5G, have higher latency than wired connections. Mobile browsers are more conservative with caching and resource loading. And most contractor websites are designed and tested on desktops, with mobile treated as an afterthought.</p>

<p>In our study, 89% of contractor websites had a mobile score more than 10 points lower than their desktop score. Only 4 websites achieved mobile scores within 5 points of their desktop scores. These 4 sites were all built with mobile-first design principles and aggressive performance optimization.</p>

